<?xml version="1.0"?>

<model>
  <name>Launch Ramp</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <description>
    Static, zero-friction launch platform for the Hirrus catapult launch.
    Two problems it solves: (1) a known, flat surface to spawn on instead
    of a heightmap terrain's collision, whose exact elevation at any given
    XY isn't something you can read off the SDF (see
    Domnesti-Slanic-5.world's own spawn-pose comment) -- spawning directly
    on a heightmap risks landing inside it; (2) zero surface friction so
    the catapult's one-shot forward impulse (model.sdf's own
    ApplyLinkWrench comment) isn't immediately fighting ground friction on
    a gear-less, belly-sliding airframe.
  </description>
</model>
